OVERVIEW: Batch compress or decompress DICOM files in a directory

Process all DICOM files in a directory, optionally recursing into
subdirectories.

Examples:
  dicom-compress batch input_dir/ --output output_dir/ --codec jpeg-lossless
  dicom-compress batch input_dir/ --output output_dir/ --codec jpeg2000
--quality high --recursive
  dicom-compress batch input_dir/ --output output_dir/ --decompress --recursive

USAGE: dicom-compress batch <input> --output <output> [--codec <codec>] [--decompress] [--quality <quality>] [--syntax <syntax>] [--recursive] [--verbose]

ARGUMENTS:
  <input>                 Input directory path

OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <output>   Output directory path
  -c, --codec <codec>     Target codec for compression (e.g., jpeg-lossless,
                          jpeg2000)
  --decompress            Decompress files instead of compressing
  -q, --quality <quality> Quality: maximum, high, medium, low, or a value
                          0.0-1.0
  -s, --syntax <syntax>   Native target syntax for decompression: explicit-le
                          (default), implicit-le, deflate, explicit-be
                          (retired) (default: explicit-le)
  -r, --recursive         Process subdirectories recursively
  --verbose               Show verbose output
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

